  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe address the Erd\u0151s discrepancy problem by minimizing the minimum overlap integral C5. The key bottleneck in existing approaches is the lack of exploitable structure in the optimization landscape. We synthesize multiple ideas: sparse representation using periodicity, smoothed binary patterns, and adaptive grid refinement. Our core innovation is the \"spiral descent\" method using exponential smoothing and interval partitioning to escape local optima. We validate against discontinuity planes and leverage the observation that optimal solutions exhibit hierarchical structure across resolutions.\n\nMathematical specification:\n- Objective: Minimize min_k \u222b_[0,2] h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx with h(x)\u2208[0,1], \u222bh(x)dx=1\n- Discretization: h defined on N=1400-5600 points, dx=2/N, requiring \u2211h_i dx=1\n- Representation: Piecewise constant on intervals defined by dyadic rationals\n- Optimization: Minimize max_k linear correlation in Macaulay brackets, subject to:\n   L1 constraint: ||h||_1 \u2264 1/dx\n   Multiplicative constraints: h(x)\u2208[0,1]\u2200x\n- Adjustment: Use constrained entropy smoothing \u03b5=0.05-0.15 to maintain feasibility\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Parent validation:\n   - Handle optional parent via `initial_h_values`\n   - Project to simplex and adjust integral at scale N0=1400 or Ninit\n2. Spiral Descent Algorithm:\n   a. Generate lattice points L={i/dx|i\u2208\u2124,0\u2264i\u22642}\n   b. Divide into K=N_sub intervals\n   c. Initialize h0 via entropy-smoothed parent projection\n   d. Create cross-validated perturbations with:\n        h_rand = random_normal(\u03bc=0.5,\u03c3=0.1)ter_clipped\n        h_sinc = sincconvolution(h0,\u03bd=0.3)ter_filtered\n   e. Run bilevel coordinate ascent with adaptive partitioning\n3. Level-wise refinement:\n   - Stage 0: Gradient flow with fixed partition size\n   - Stage 1: Progressive subdivision with adaptive \u03b5-smoothing\n   - Stage 2: Multi-scale optimization with entropy constraints\n4. Stopping criteria:\n   - |\u2207C5|<10\u207b\u2076 or |new_C5 - old_C5|<10\u207b\u2079\n   - Resolution maxed at N=5600\n   - Time: 1000 seconds max per resolution level\n\nSearch choices and use case variations:\n1. Base optimization:\n   - N_start=1400\n   - Max subdivisions=5 (current record)\n   - Subdivision kernel: Gaussian smoothing with \u03c3_adaptive\n   - Initial config: `{'dx':2/1400, '\u03b5_smooth':0.1, 'proj_nit':3}`\n   - Termination: either improvement threshold or iteration count\n2. Hyperparameter tuning variations:\n   a. Noise level sweep: \u03b1\u2208[0.05,0.2,0.35]\n   b. Entropy coefficient sweep: \u03b2\u2208[0.01,0.05,0.1]\n   c. Coarsening strategy: disable noise/keep/disable smoothing\n3. Parallel execution variant: `sweep_cv=True` runs 5 concurrent trials\n\nBudget and robustness:\n- Time estimate: ~600-800s across levels; watch 30s milestones\n- Hardware: Multiprocessing with 4-8 cores\n- Resource usage: Max. 32GB RAM (avoid large correlation matrices)\n- Fallback mechanism: For failed iterations, revert to clipped polar harmonic basis\n- Output validation:\n   - Integral: |\u2211h_i*dx - 1| < 1e-6\n   - Values: min(h_i)>=0, max(h_i)<=1\n   - Correlation: double-check via scipy.fft\n\nValidation and return contract:\n1. Precompute: \n   - projected_h = project_feasible(best_h, len(best_h))\n   - verify \u2211projected_h*dx exactly equals 1\n2. Score computation:\n   - c5 = max(np.correlate(projected_h, 1-projected_h, mode='full')) * dx\n   - ensure \u221e-norm < warning threshold if exceptional\n3. Early stopping conditions:\n   - Time remaining < 20s & improvement < 1e-8\n   - Entropy degradation (when projected entropy > stable threshold)\n4. Fallback restoration:\n   - If optimization invalidates solution, restore via: \n        h_safe = np.clip(best_h,0,1); adjust_integral(h_safe)\n   - For expanded parents, use: \n        dx_new = 2/N_new; factor = N_old/2/dx_old; adjust h accordingly\n5. Structured output:\n   - Return (h_values, best_c5, n_points) as np.array(intervals)\n   - Ensure final correlation re-computed exactly",
